"cost-of-cctv-installation-uae": {
"slug": "cost-of-cctv-installation-uae",
"title": "How much does CCTV installation cost in the UAE? (2026 price guide)",
"excerpt": "A CCTV installation in the UAE typically costs AED 350–900 per camera (supply + install). A 4-camera HD package runs about AED 1,500–3,500 and an 8-camera setup AED 2,800–6,500, including the recorder. 4K/IP systems cost more. In Dubai many premises must use SIRA-approved equipment — get free, comparable quotes on QuotesDone.",
"meta_desc": "UAE CCTV costs: AED 350–900/camera, 4-cam package AED 1,500–3,500, 8-cam AED 2,800–6,500. SIRA notes. Indicative 2026 ranges.",
"body_html": "<p>CCTV is priced by camera count, resolution and cabling &mdash; and in Dubai, by whether the equipment and installer are SIRA-approved. This 2026 guide gives real ranges plus the compliance point most quotes leave out.</p><p>Ranges are indicative across the Emirates. For a firm number, <a href=\"/app\">get free, comparable quotes</a>.</p><h2>Typical CCTV prices in the UAE (2026)</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Indicative price (AED)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Per camera &mdash; HD (supply + install)</td><td>350&ndash;900</td></tr><tr><td>Per camera &mdash; 4K / IP</td><td>700&ndash;1,500</td></tr><tr><td>4-camera HD package</td><td>1,500&ndash;3,500</td></tr><tr><td>8-camera HD package</td><td>2,800&ndash;6,500</td></tr><tr><td>8-camera 4K / IP package</td><td>6,000&ndash;12,000</td></tr><tr><td>16-camera package</td><td>5,500&ndash;14,000</td></tr><tr><td>NVR / DVR + storage</td><td>600&ndash;2,500</td></tr><tr><td>Annual maintenance (AMC)</td><td>500&ndash;2,000</td></tr></tbody></table><p style=\"color:#9DB2B2;font-size:13px\">Indicative ranges only &mdash; resolution, cabling and storage change the number.</p><h2>Dubai: SIRA compliance</h2><p>In Dubai, many commercial premises &mdash; and some residential ones &mdash; must use SIRA-approved cameras, recorders and installers, with a set number of days of recording retained. A compliant quote should name the approved installer and the retention period. This is a common reason a cheaper quote is not comparable to a compliant one.</p><h2>What drives the price</h2><ul><li>Camera count and resolution (HD vs 4K/IP)</li><li>Cable runs, conduits and trunking</li><li>Days of recording storage</li><li>SIRA-approved equipment and installer (Dubai)</li><li>Remote viewing, night vision and analytics</li></ul><h2>Red flags when comparing CCTV quotes</h2><ul><li>No-name recorder or cameras with no warranty</li><li>No SIRA line where your premises require it</li><li>Storage days not stated &mdash; you may only get 2&ndash;3 days of footage</li><li>&ldquo;Per camera&rdquo; price that excludes cabling and the recorder</li></ul><h2>FAQs</h2><div class=\"faq\"><b>Do I need SIRA approval for CCTV in Dubai?</b><div>Many commercial and some residential installs in Dubai must use SIRA-approved equipment and installers. Reputable suppliers handle this &mdash; flag it when you request quotes.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>HD vs IP/4K cameras?</b><div>IP/4K give sharper footage and analytics but cost more and need more storage; HD is cheaper for basic coverage.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>How many cameras do I need?</b><div>Most villas use 4&ndash;8 cameras covering entries and the perimeter; suppliers advise based on your layout.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>How many days of footage should I keep?</b><div>Home setups often keep 7&ndash;14 days; SIRA-regulated premises in Dubai have a required minimum &mdash; confirm it in the quote.</div></div><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do I need SIRA approval for CCTV in Dubai?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Many commercial and some residential installs in Dubai must use SIRA-approved equipment and installers. Reputable suppliers handle this, flag it when you request quotes.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"HD or IP/4K CCTV cameras?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"IP/4K give sharper footage and analytics but cost more and need more storage; HD is cheaper for basic coverage.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How many CCTV cameras does a villa need?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Most villas use 4 to 8 cameras covering entries and the perimeter; suppliers advise based on your layout.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How many days of CCTV footage should I keep?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Home setups often keep 7 to 14 days; SIRA-regulated premises in Dubai have a required minimum, confirm it in the quote.\"}}]}</script><p style=\"border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);margin-top:22px;padding-top:16px\"><b>Ready to get quotes?</b> Compare <a href=\"/services/cctv-security/\">CCTV &amp; security suppliers across the UAE</a> anonymously on QuotesDone. Related: <a href=\"/blog/cost-of-smart-home-uae/\">smart-home automation costs</a>.</p>",
"author": "QuotesDone",
"category": "Cost guides",
"published_at": "2026-06-28T20:51:06.189058+00:00",
"sort": 44
