"title": "How much does plumbing cost in the UAE? (2026 price guide)",
"excerpt": "In the UAE, a plumber call-out is about AED 100–250, a tap/mixer replacement AED 80–300, a water heater supply + install AED 600–2,000, and leak detection AED 250–800. A full bathroom re-plumb runs AED 2,500–8,000. Price depends on the job — get free, comparable quotes on QuotesDone.",
"meta_desc": "UAE plumbing costs: call-out AED 100–250, water heater AED 600–2,000, leak detection AED 250–800, bathroom re-plumb AED 2,500–8,000. Indicative 2026 ranges.",
"body_html": "<p>Plumbing is priced by call-out, per fixture, or per project &mdash; and finding a hidden leak is where prices jump. This 2026 guide shows fair ranges.</p><p>Ranges are indicative across the Emirates. For a firm number, <a href=\"/app\">get free, comparable quotes</a>.</p><h2>Typical plumbing prices in the UAE (2026)</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Indicative price (AED)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Plumber call-out</td><td>100&ndash;250</td></tr><tr><td>Tap / mixer replacement</td><td>80&ndash;300</td></tr><tr><td>Water heater (supply + install)</td><td>600&ndash;2,000</td></tr><tr><td>Leak detection</td><td>250&ndash;800</td></tr><tr><td>Blocked drain clearing</td><td>150&ndash;600</td></tr><tr><td>Full bathroom re-plumb</td><td>2,500&ndash;8,000</td></tr></tbody></table><p style=\"color:#9DB2B2;font-size:13px\">Indicative ranges only &mdash; the job, access and parts change the number.</p><h2>What drives the price</h2><ul><li>Nature of the job (fix vs install vs re-plumb)</li><li>Parts and fixture grade</li><li>Access behind walls or under floors</li><li>Leak detection vs a simple repair</li><li>Emergency / after-hours call-out</li></ul><h2>Included vs extra</h2><ul><li><b>Usually included:</b> labour and basic fittings.</li><li><b>Usually extra:</b> fixtures and heaters, opening and making good walls/floors, specialist leak detection.</li></ul><h2>Red flags when comparing quotes</h2><ul><li>Repeated patch fixes instead of finding the leak source</li><li>Making-good not quoted</li><li>No warranty on the repair</li><li>Cash job with no invoice</li></ul><h2>FAQs</h2><div class=\"faq\"><b>Signs of a hidden leak?</b><div>Rising water bills, damp patches, or a drop in pressure.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Is making-good included?</b><div>Usually extra &mdash; opening and re-finishing walls or floors is a separate line.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>How long does a bathroom re-plumb take?</b><div>A few days, plus tiling and finishing re