"title": "How much do movers cost in the UAE? (2026 price guide)",
"excerpt": "In the UAE, a studio move typically costs AED 300–700, a 1-bedroom AED 500–1,200, a 2-bedroom AED 900–2,200, and a villa AED 2,500–8,000. Packing materials and storage are extra. Price depends on size, distance and floors — get free, comparable quotes on QuotesDone.",
"meta_desc": "UAE moving costs: studio AED 300–700, 1BR AED 500–1,200, 2BR AED 900–2,200, villa AED 2,500–8,000. Indicative 2026 ranges.",
"body_html": "<p>Moving prices in the UAE scale with home size, distance and access &mdash; and home size alone drives roughly 40% of the total. This 2026 guide shows real ranges so a &ldquo;from AED 300&rdquo; ad does not turn into a surprise on the day.</p><p>Ranges are indicative across the Emirates. For a firm number, <a href=\"/app\">get free, comparable quotes</a>.</p><h2>Typical moving prices in the UAE (2026)</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Move</th><th>Indicative price (AED)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Studio</td><td>500&ndash;1,000</td></tr><tr><td>1-bedroom</td><td>800&ndash;1,500</td></tr><tr><td>2-bedroom apartment</td><td>1,300&ndash;2,500</td></tr><tr><td>3-bedroom / small villa</td><td>2,500&ndash;5,000</td></tr><tr><td>4&ndash;5 bedroom villa</td><td>4,500&ndash;9,000</td></tr><tr><td>Packing materials</td><td>150&ndash;600</td></tr><tr><td>Storage (per month)</td><td>200&ndash;800</td></tr></tbody></table><p style=\"color:#9DB2B2;font-size:13px\">Indicative ranges only &mdash; volume, distance and access change the number.</p><h2>How distance changes the price (2-bed example)</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>Indicative price (AED)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Within the same community</td><td>1,300&ndash;1,800</td></tr><tr><td>Across the city</td><td>1,800&ndash;2,600</td></tr><tr><td>Cross-emirate (e.g. Dubai &rarr; Abu Dhabi)</td><td>2,600&ndash;3,500</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What is usually included</h2><ul><li>Loading, transport and unloading</li><li>Basic dismantling and reassembly of beds and wardrobes</li><li>Blankets and basic protection for furniture</li></ul><h2>What usually costs extra</h2><ul><li>Full packing materials and labour</li><li>Storage between move-out and move-in</li><li>Handyman work: curtains, TV mounts, light fittings</li><li>Difficult access: high floors, long carry, no lift</li></ul><h2>Red flags when comparing moving quotes</h2><ul><li>A price quoted without a photo or video survey of your home</li><li>Vague &ldquo;starting from&rdquo; pricing with no fixed total</li><li>No mention of insurance or liability for damage</li><li>Cash-only with no written confirmation of scope</li></ul><h2>FAQs</h2><div class=\"faq\"><b>Is packing included?</b><div>Sometimes &mdash; confirm whether packing materials and labour are in the quote or charged separately.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Do movers dismantle furniture?</b><div>Most do basic dismantling and reassembly of beds and wardrobes; confirm for complex or imported items.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Do inter-emirate moves cost more?</b><div>Yes &mdash; distance and time add to the price. A 2-bed cross-emirate move typically runs AED 2,600&ndash;3,500.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Should the mover survey my home first?</b><div>Yes. A quick photo or video survey is how you get an accurate fixed price instead of a guess.</div></div><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is packing included in a UAE moving quote?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Sometimes, confirm whether packing materials and labour are in the quote or charged separately.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do movers dismantle furniture?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Most do basic dismantling and reassembly of beds and wardrobes; confirm for complex or imported items.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do inter-emirate moves cost more?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, distance and time add to the price. A 2-bed cross-emirate move typically runs AED 2,600 to 3,500.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Should the mover survey my home first?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. A quick photo or video survey is how you get an accurate fixed price instead of a guess.\"}}]}</script><p style=\"border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);margin-top:22px;padding-top:16px\"><b>Ready to get quotes?</b> Compare <a href=\"/services/movers/\">movers &amp; packers across the UAE</a> anonymously on QuotesDone.</p>",
