"title": "Building & fit-out material prices in the UAE (2026): steel, MDF, acrylic, glass & more",
"excerpt": "Indicative UAE material prices: reinforcement steel about AED 2,200–3,200 per ton, MDF (18mm) AED 60–120 per sheet, acrylic sheet AED 60–180 per sqm, clear glass (6mm) AED 35–90 per sqm and cement AED 12–18 per bag. Commodity prices move weekly — get live, comparable quotes on QuotesDone.",
"meta_desc": "UAE building material prices 2026: steel ~AED 2,200–3,200/ton, MDF AED 60–120/sheet, acrylic AED 60–180/sqm, glass AED 35–90/sqm, cement AED 12–18/bag. Indicative.",
"body_html": "<p>If you are buying materials directly — for a project, a workshop or trade resale — here are indicative UAE price ranges for the most common items. Steel, aluminium and other metals track global commodity markets, so treat these as starting points and confirm current rates with live quotes.</p><h2>Structural & civil materials</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Indicative price (AED)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Reinforcement steel (rebar)</td><td>2,200–3,200 / ton</td></tr><tr><td>Structural steel (I/H beams, sections)</td><td>2,800–4,500 / ton</td></tr><tr><td>Mild steel plate / sheet</td><td>3–6 / kg</td></tr><tr><td>Stainless steel sheet (304)</td><td>18–35 / kg</td></tr><tr><td>Cement (OPC, 50 kg bag)</td><td>12–18 / bag</td></tr><tr><td>Ready-mix concrete</td><td>180–320 / m³</td></tr><tr><td>Sand</td><td>40–90 / m³</td></tr><tr><td>Aggregate / gravel</td><td>50–110 / m³</td></tr><tr><td>Hollow concrete blocks</td><td>1.5–4 / piece</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Boards & wood</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Indicative price (AED)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>MDF board (18mm, 4x8 ft sheet)</td><td>60–120 / sheet</td></tr><tr><td>Moisture-resistant MDF (HMR)</td><td>90–180 / sheet</td></tr><tr><td>Commercial plywood (18mm, 4x8)</td><td>70–160 / sheet</td></tr><tr><td>Marine plywood (18mm)</td><td>120–300 / sheet</td></tr><tr><td>Gypsum board (12.5mm)</td><td>20–45 / sheet</td></tr><tr><td>Blockboard / chipboard</td><td>50–130 / sheet</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Sheets & glazing</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Indicative price (AED)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Acrylic sheet (cast, 3mm)</td><td>60–180 / sqm</td></tr><tr><td>Acrylic sheet (10mm)</td><td>180–450 / sqm</td></tr><tr><td>Clear float glass (6mm)</td><td>35–90 / sqm</td></tr><tr><td>Tempered glass (10mm)</td><td>90–250 / sqm</td></tr><tr><td>Aluminium composite panel (ACP)</td><td>60–180 / sqm</td></tr><tr><td>Aluminium profile / extrusion</td><td>14–28 / kg</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Finishing materials</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Indicative price (AED)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ceramic tiles (material only)</td><td>20–80 / sqm</td></tr><tr><td>Porcelain tiles (material only)</td><td>35–150 / sqm</td></tr><tr><td>Emulsion paint (gallon, ~3.6 L)</td><td>35–120</td></tr><tr><td>Emulsion paint (18 L drum)</td><td>150–500</td></tr></tbody></table><p style=\"font-size:13px;color:#9DB2B2\"><b>Important:</b> Raw-material prices in the UAE move with global commodity markets, exchange rates and order quantity, and differ between wholesale and retail. Treat these as indicative starting points — confirm today''s rates by <a href=\"/app\">getting live quotes</a>.</p><h2>What affects material prices</h2><ul><li>Global commodity markets (steel, aluminium, copper) and shipping</li><li>Order quantity — bulk/trade orders get better rates than retail</li><li>Grade, thickness, brand and finish</li><li>Delivery, cutting and handling</li></ul><h2>FAQs</h2><div class=\"faq\"><b>Why do UAE material prices change so often?</b><div>Metals like steel and aluminium track global commodity markets and freight, so prices can move week to week. Cement, sand and aggregates are usually more stable.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Are these wholesale or retail prices?</b><div>They are indicative trade/wholesale ranges. Small retail quantities cost more; bulk orders get better rates.</div></div><div class=\"faq\"><b>Can I source materials through QuotesDone?</b><div>Yes — describe the materials and quantities you need and material suppliers and traders send quotes to compare, anonymously.</div></div><p><a href=\"/app\">Get free material quotes →</a></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Why do UAE building material prices change so often?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Metals like steel and aluminium track global commodity markets and freight, so prices can move week to week. Cement, sand and aggregates are usually more stable.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Are these wholesale or retail material prices?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"They are indicative trade or wholesale ranges. Small retail quantities cost more; bulk orders get better rates.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I source building materials through QuotesDone?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes — describe the materials and quantities you need and material suppliers and traders send quotes to compare, anonymously.\"}}]}</script>",
