"how-much-does-an-annual-ac-maintenance-contract-cost-in-the-uae-2026-p": {
"slug": "how-much-does-an-annual-ac-maintenance-contract-cost-in-the-uae-2026-p",
"title": "How much does an annual AC maintenance contract cost in the UAE? (2026 price guide)",
"excerpt": "What should you pay for an annual AC maintenance contract in the UAE in 2026? Real price ranges per unit, what a good AMC covers, and how to compare quotes without overpaying.",
"meta_desc": "2026 UAE guide to annual AC maintenance contract (AMC) prices per split, ducted and central unit, plus what's included and how to compare quotes fairly.",
"body_html": "<p>An annual maintenance contract (AMC) keeps your air conditioning running efficiently, cuts the risk of a mid-summer breakdown, and spreads the cost across the year. But AMC pricing in the UAE varies wildly depending on unit type, number of units, and what the contract actually includes. Here is a practical 2026 breakdown for SMEs, retail units, offices and villas.</p>\n\n<h2>Typical AC maintenance contract prices in the UAE (2026)</h2>\n<p>AMCs are usually priced per unit per year, with a set number of scheduled visits. As a working guide:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Split / wall-mounted unit:</strong> AED 250-500 per unit per year (typically 2-4 visits).</li>\n<li><strong>Cassette / ceiling unit:</strong> AED 350-650 per unit per year.</li>\n<li><strong>Ducted / concealed split:</strong> AED 500-900 per unit per year (more filters and duct access).</li>\n<li><strong>Package / rooftop unit:</strong> AED 900-2,000 per unit per year.</li>\n<li><strong>Central / chilled water (FCU + AHU):</strong> priced per system, often AED 3,000-15,000+ per year depending on tonnage and building size.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Small offices and villas with 3-6 split units commonly land between AED 1,200 and AED 3,000 per year for a comprehensive contract. Retail and F&B units with heavier loads pay more because units run longer hours.</p>\n\n<h3>Comprehensive vs non-comprehensive contracts</h3>\n<p>This is the single biggest reason two quotes differ by hundreds of dirhams:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Non-comprehensive (labour only):</strong> covers scheduled servicing and callouts, but you pay for spare parts, gas top-ups and compressors separately. Cheaper upfront.</li>\n<li><strong>Comprehensive:</strong> includes most parts, refrigerant top-ups and some repairs. Higher price, fewer surprise bills. Read exclusions carefully, compressors are often still excluded.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What a good AC maintenance contract should include</h2>\n<p>Before you compare prices, agree on scope. A solid AMC should cover:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Scheduled preventive visits (state how many per year and roughly when).</li>\n<li>Filter cleaning or replacement at each visit.</li>\n<li>Coil cleaning, drain line clearing and gas pressure checks.</li>\n<li>Electrical connection and thermostat checks.</li>\n<li>Emergency callout response time (e.g. within 24-48 hours).</li>\n<li>A service report after each visit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Note what is <em>not</em> included: compressor replacement, major duct cleaning, and gas refills beyond a top-up are common exclusions.</p>\n\n<h2>What drives your AMC price up or down</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Number of units:</strong> more units usually means a lower per-unit rate.</li>\n<li><strong>Unit type and age:</strong> older or ducted systems need more labour and parts.</li>\n<li><strong>Operating hours:</strong> a restaurant or clinic running 16 hours a day wears units faster than a 9-to-5 office.</li>\n<li><strong>Visit frequency:</strong> 4 visits a year costs more than 2, but is worth it in the Gulf climate.</li>\n<li><strong>Response guarantees:</strong> faster emergency response and after-hours cover add a premium.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>How to compare AC maintenance quotes fairly</h2>\n<p>Cheap AMCs often hide their value in the exclusions. To compare like for like:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>List every unit by type and location so all suppliers quote the same scope.</li>\n<li>Ask for price <em>per unit per year</em>, not just a lump sum.</li>\n<li>Confirm the number of visits and whether callouts are included or charged.</li>\n<li>Ask what parts are covered and get exclusions in writing.</li>\n<li>Check the response time commitment and whether it is genuinely guaranteed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The fastest way to get comparable numbers is to describe your setup once and let verified UAE suppliers quote against the same brief. On QuotesDone you can post the job and <a href=\"https://quotesdone.com/app\">get anonymous quotes</a> from vetted providers, so pricing stays honest and you are not chased by sales calls before you have decided. You only pay a 3% reveal fee on the quote you actually accept.</p>\n<p>If you also need one-off servicing or duct work alongside your contract, our <a href=\"https://quotesdone.com/\">AC maintenance and cleaning services</a> can be quoted together to save on callouts.</p>\n\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n<h3>How many AC service visits do I need per year in the UAE?</h3>\n<p>Two to four is standard. Homes and light-use offices manage on two, while retail, clinics and F&B with heavy usage benefit from three or four to keep coils clean and efficiency high during peak summer.</p>\n\n<h3>Is a comprehensive AMC worth the extra cost?</h3>\n<p>If your units are more than five years old or run long hours, comprehensive cover usually pays off by absorbing part costs. For newer units under warranty, a non-comprehensive labour-only contract is often enough.</p>\n\n<h3>Does an AMC cover a full compressor replacement?</h3>\n<p>Rarely. Compressors are the most expensive component and are almost always excluded, even in comprehensive contracts. Always confirm this in writing before signing.</p>",
"author": "QuotesDone Team",
"category": "Cost Guides",
"published_at": "2026-07-04T22:42:41.289347+00:00",
"sort": 65
},
"how-much-does-office-partition-installation-cost-in-the-uae-2026-price": {
"slug": "how-much-does-office-partition-installation-cost-in-the-uae-2026-price",
"title": "How much does office partition installation cost in the UAE? (2026 price guide)",
"excerpt": "A clear 2026 breakdown of office partition costs in the UAE — glass, gypsum and demountable systems, price ranges per square metre, and how to compare quotes.",
"meta_desc": "2026 UAE office partition cost guide: glass, gypsum & demountable partition prices per sqm, what drives the cost, and how to compare quotes fairly.",
"body_html": "<p>Reconfiguring an office in Dubai, Abu Dhabi or Sharjah almost always comes down to one question: how do we split the space? Partitions are the fastest way to create meeting rooms, private offices and quiet zones without a full fit-out. This 2026 guide breaks down realistic UAE partition prices, what moves the cost, and how to compare quotes without getting caught out.</p><h2>Typical office partition costs in the UAE (2026)</h2><p>Prices are usually quoted per square metre of partition wall (height x length), supplied and installed. As a working reference for the UAE market in 2026:</p><ul><li><strong>Gypsum (drywall) partitions:</strong> roughly AED 90–180 per sqm for a standard single-stud, double-boarded wall. Add insulation and acoustic board and you move toward the top of that range.</li><li><strong>Aluminium-framed glass partitions:</strong> roughly AED 350–650 per sqm depending on glass thickness, frame profile and finish.</li><li><strong>Frameless / structural glass partitions:</strong> roughly AED 600–1,100 per sqm, higher for double-glazed acoustic glass.</li><li><strong>Demountable / modular systems (imported):</strong> roughly AED 900–2,000+ per sqm — premium because panels are reusable and relocatable.</li></ul><p>Doors, blinds, film, and any electrical or ELV routing inside the partition are usually priced separately, so always check whether they are included.</p><h3>Which type suits which need?</h3><ul><li><strong>Gypsum</strong> — best value for solid private offices and stores where you do not need light or a view through.</li><li><strong>Glass</strong> — the choice for a modern, open feel; good for meeting rooms and manager cabins that still need light.</li><li><strong>Demountable</strong> — worth it if your business relocates or reconfigures often, since the panels can be dismantled and reused.</li></ul><h2>What actually drives the price</h2><p>Two quotes for the same room can differ widely, and it is rarely just markup. The main cost drivers are:</p><ul><li><strong>Glass specification:</strong> 10mm vs 12mm, single vs double glazing, and acoustic laminated glass all change the number significantly.</li><li><strong>Acoustic rating:</strong> proper sound insulation (insulation infill, sealed head/base tracks, acoustic seals on glass) adds material and labour.</li><li><strong>Height:</strong> partitions running to a high slab or above a false ceiling cost more than those stopping at ceiling level.</li><li><strong>Doors and hardware:</strong> hinged, sliding or frameless glass doors with floor springs and closers can add several thousand dirhams each.</li><li><strong>Finishes:</strong> paint-ready gypsum vs skimmed and painted, powder-coated frame colours, and manifestation film all add up.</li><li><strong>Site conditions and access:</strong> occupied offices, after-hours work, and buildings requiring fit-out permits and NOCs push labour costs higher.</li></ul><h2>Don't forget permits and building rules</h2><p>Most UAE commercial towers and free zones require approval before you alter the layout. That can mean a fit-out permit, landlord NOC, and compliance with civil defence rules for fire exits and sprinkler coverage. A partition that blocks an emergency route or a sprinkler head will be rejected. A good contractor prices this in and handles the drawings; a cheap quote that ignores it can cost you more later.</p><h2>How to compare partition quotes fairly</h2><p>To compare like for like, make sure every quote states:</p><ul><li>Partition type and exact glass thickness / gypsum build-up</li><li>Total square metres and linear metres</li><li>Acoustic rating (if any)</li><li>Doors, hardware and film — included or excluded</li><li>Permits, NOCs and civil defence approval responsibility</li><li>Making good, painting and cleanup</li><li>Warranty and expected timeline</li></ul><p>The easiest way to get several genuine, comparable numbers is to describe the job once and let suppliers quote against the same brief. On QuotesDone you can <a href=\"https://quotesdone.com/app\">get anonymous quotes</a> from verified UAE suppliers who compete without knowing who you are — so pricing stays honest and you are not stuck with the one contractor a colleague recommended. You only pay a 3% reveal fee on the quote you actually choose to accept. If you are also changing the ceiling grid at the same time, our <a href=\"https://quotesdone.com/\">fit-out and interior services</a> can be quoted together to save mobilisation costs.</p><h2>Ways to keep the cost sensible</h2><ul><li>Combine partition work with painting or ceiling changes to share site setup and labour.</li><li>Use gypsum where privacy matters more than light, and reserve glass for feature rooms.</li><li>Ask for a mix — glass fronts with gypsum returns often looks premium at a lower cost.</li><li>Schedule after-hours only where it is truly necessary; night rates carry a premium.</li></ul><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>How long does office partition installation take?</h3><p>A single meeting room can be installed in one to two days. A full floor reconfiguration with glass and doors typically runs one to three weeks, plus lead time for imported glass or demountable systems and any permit approvals.</p><h3>Are glass partitions worth the extra cost over gypsum?</h3><p>If natural light, an open feel and a modern look matter, glass is usually worth it. For pure privacy or storage rooms where a view through adds nothing, gypsum delivers the same function for a fraction of the price.</p><h3>Do I need civil defence approval for office partitions?</h3><p>Often yes. Any change that affects fire exits, escape routes or sprinkler coverage generally requires fit-out permit and civil defence sign-off in UAE commercial buildings. Confirm who is responsible for approvals before signing.</p>",
