"html": "<nav class=\"nav\"><a href=\"/terms/\" class=\"\">Terms of Service</a><a href=\"/privacy/\" class=\"\">Privacy Policy</a><a href=\"/supplier-agreement/\" class=\"\">Supplier Agreement</a><a href=\"/cookie-policy/\" class=\"on\">Cookie Policy</a><a href=\"/refund-policy/\" class=\"\">Refund & Cancellation</a><a href=\"/acceptable-use/\" class=\"\">Acceptable Use</a><a href=\"/disclaimer/\" class=\"\">Disclaimer</a><a href=\"/complaints/\" class=\"\">Complaints & Disputes</a></nav><article class=\"doc\"><div class=\"dochead\"><h1>Cookie Policy</h1><div class=\"meta\">QuotesDone Technologies · Version v6 · Last updated 29 June 2026</div><div class=\"meta\">The English version of this document is the governing version.</div></div><div class=\"body\"><h1>Cookie Policy</h1><div class=\"muted\">How QuotesDone uses cookies and similar technologies, how we obtain consent consistent with UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021, and how you can manage or disable them.</div><div class=\"card\"><h2>1. About This Policy</h2><p>This Cookie Policy explains how QuotesDone Technologies (Dubai DET E-Trader Licence No. 1633275) uses cookies and similar technologies on the QuotesDone platform. It should be read together with our Privacy Policy.</p><p>Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. Similar technologies include local storage, pixels and tags that perform comparable functions.</p><p>Where cookies collect or relate to personal data, we handle that data in accordance with the UAE Personal Data Protection Law, Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 (PDPL). This policy tells you which cookies we use, why, and how you can control them. By using the platform after being shown our cookie notice, and where required after giving consent, you agree to the use of cookies as described here.</p><h2>2. Cookies We Use</h2><p>We use the following categories:</p><ul><li>Essential and session cookies: necessary to run the platform, keep you signed in, remember your request as you build it, and enable core features such as paid reveals. The platform cannot function properly without these.</li><li>Security cookies: help us verify sessions, support OTP-based mobile verification, detect fraud and protect the platform and your account.</li><li>Analytics cookies: help us understand how the platform is used so we can improve performance and matching. These may be set by trusted analytics providers and are used in an aggregated or pseudonymised manner where possible.</li></ul><p>We do not use cookies to build advertising profiles or to sell your data.</p><h2>3. Consent Approach</h2><p>Our approach to cookie consent is consistent with the PDPL:</p><ul><li>Essential and security cookies are strictly necessary for the service and are set without requiring separate consent, because they are required to deliver the service you request.</li><li>Analytics and other non-essential cookies are only used where we have an appropriate lawful basis, and where consent is required we obtain it through our cookie notice before those cookies are set.</li><li>You can accept or decline non-essential cookies, and you can change your choice at any time.</li></ul><p>Withdrawing consent or declining non-essential cookies will not prevent you from using the core features of QuotesDone, although some functionality and our ability to improve the service may be affected.</p><h2>4. Managing and Disabling Cookies</h2><p>You can control cookies in several ways:</p><ul><li>Use the cookie notice or settings on our platform to accept or decline non-essential categories and to update your preferences.</li><li>Adjust your browser settings to block or delete cookies, or to warn you before cookies are stored. Most browsers allow this through their privacy or settings menu.</li><li>Use your device or browser&#x27;s controls for local storage and similar technologies.</li></ul><p>Please note that blocking essential or security cookies may stop parts of the platform from working, including sign-in, request submission and paid reveals. Disabling analytics cookies will not affect core functionality.</p><p>For help managing cookies, contact us at management@quotesdone.com.</p><h2>5. Third-Party Tags</h2><p>Some cookies and tags are set by third parties that provide services to us:</p><ul><li>Analytics providers, which help us measure and improve how the platform performs.</li><li>Our third-party payment processor, which may set cookies or use similar technologies to process card and Apple Pay payments securely and to prevent payment fraud during the reveal and payment flows.</li></ul><p>These third parties process data under their own terms and policies and, where they act for us, under written instructions. We share only what is needed for the relevant service. We encourage you to review the privacy and cookie notices of any third-party services you interact with through the platform.</p><h2>6. Changes and Contact</h2><p>We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the technologies we use or in applicable law. The current version is always available on our platform, and the effective date will be updated when we make changes.</p><p>If you have any questions about our use of cookies or wish to exercise your data protection rights under the PDPL, please contact:</p><ul><li>QuotesDone Technologies</li><li>Email: management@quotesdone.com</li><li>Phone: +971 56 791 8605</li><li>Address: Dubai, United Arab Emirates</li></ul><p>This policy is governed by the laws of the UAE, and any disputes are subject to the courts of Dubai.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"note\"><b>Operator:</b> QuotesDone Technologies, Dubai DET E-Trader (Professional) Licence No. 1633275, Commercial Register No. 2883503, Dubai, UAE. <b>Governing law:</b> the laws of the United Arab Emirates, including the Commercial Transactions Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 50 of 2022), the Electronic Transactions and Trust Services Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021), the Consumer Protection Law (Federal Law No. 15 of 2020) and Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023, the Personal Data Protection Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021), and the Civil Transactions Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 25 of 2025, in force from 1 June 2026). Disputes are subject to the competent courts of Dubai.</div>\n</article>"
